  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 144 PM CDT Thu Aug 13 2026\n\nFrontrange thunderstorms due to easterly surface flow on the north \nside of a surface low pressure system will be the story of the \nweekend. Whether steering flow will bring these thunderstorms into \nour CWA remains the biggest question in the long term. However, if \nthese storms are top make it into the northwestern combined \nPanhandles, strong wind gusts could be an impact to keep an eye on \nwith the environment in place. \n\nAfter the weekend, the story largely remains the same as the upper-\nlevel high pressure retrogrades back west, placing the Panhandles in \nanother high-pressure regime with hot daily maximum temperatures and \ndry conditions. Although, the flow does flatten out over the central \nUS, with consistent W flow over the rockies as we head into mid-next \nweek. Lee side shortwave perturbations could bring some weather to \nthe OK and northern TX Panhandles mid-next week if this pattern \nholds. \n\nFerguson",
